//
//	 0  sequence u64    written **last** by the producer with release semantics after the payload is written.
//	                    Odd = being written, even = ready. A consumer reading an odd value skips it.
//	 8  payload_length u32  must be <= slot_size; **the consumer must check this itself**
//	12  flags u32
//	16  monotonic_timestamp_nanos u64
//	24  reserved, must be 0
//
// # Rules for untrusted input (implementations must follow them)
//
//  1. payload_length is always compared with the slot_size from the control plane before use; if it exceeds it, drop the
//     slot and count one protocol error. Don't clamp and keep reading; that would turn a bug into silent
//     data corruption.
//  2. The peer's cursor is untrusted. When advancing, the consumer must check
//     producer_cursor - consumer_cursor <= slot_count; exceeding it means the producer lapped it,
//     and it should jump to the latest lap rather than read a batch of slots that were already overwritten.
//  3. When slot_count / slot_size / descriptor_bytes in the header disagree with the control plane,
